    {
      "id": "eb6u3ut",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Natural vegetation in India is determined primarily by variations in rainfall, temperature, altitude, and soil types.",
        "Tropical Deciduous Forests, also known as Monsoon Forests, represent the most widespread vegetation cover in India.",
        "Tropical Evergreen Forests occur in areas with over 200 cm of rainfall and lack a distinct leaf-shedding season.",
        "Montane vegetation varies distinctly with altitude, ranging from wet temperate forests to high-altitude alpine vegetation.",
        "Mangrove forests are specialized coastal vegetation adapted to saline tidal waters, predominantly located in river deltas."
      ],
      "id": "7sjtvgx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rd84g6y",
      "content": "• Climate – Temperature and rainfall determine vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d4c7mkm",
      "content": "• Soil – Different soils support different plants."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rzzagnr",
      "content": "• Relief – Plains, plateaus and mountains influence vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5xa73lo",
      "content": "• Altitude – Vegetation changes with height in mountain regions."
    },
    {
