    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Tropical Deciduous forests are sub-classified into Moist Deciduous (100–200 cm rain) and Dry Deciduous (70–100 cm rain).",
        "Teak and Sal are the two most important commercial timber species of Tropical Deciduous forests.",
        "The Sundarbans, the world's largest mangrove forest, gets its name from the predominant 'Sundari' tree species."
      ],
      "id": "i4ryxnu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dyvvdy5",
      "content": "• Prevents soil erosion."
    },
